WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:17.717
Sun and his companions woke up in a meadow.

2
00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:23.622
Bees buzzed and birds sang as leaves rustled in a gentle breeze.

3
00:00:28.606 --> 00:00:30.668
a lovely day," the Tang Monk said.

4
00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:37.106
"Just wait until you see the Western Paradise, Master," Wukong said.

5
00:00:37.126 --> 00:00:40.347
"The weather is always beautiful there."

6
00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:44.789
"I can't wait, so let's start walking," the monk said.

7
00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:48.171
"I'll prepare the horse," Wujing said.

8
00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:53.513
Bajie lay asleep, drooling with his mouth open.

9
00:00:56.214 --> 00:00:57.595
Wukong shook Bajie.

10
00:00:57.615 --> 00:00:58.395
"Wake up!"

11
00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:00.296
Bajie rolled over.

12
00:01:02.264 --> 00:01:03.365
"Get up, lazy!"

13
00:01:03.645 --> 00:01:04.946
Wukong kicked Bajie.

14
00:01:04.966 --> 00:01:08.208
"Ouch!" Bajie cried, jumping up.

15
00:01:08.228 --> 00:01:10.330
"Why did you do that?"

16
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.752
"You didn't get up," Wukong said.

17
00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:17.615
"You didn't ask politely," Bajie said.

18
00:01:17.635 --> 00:01:20.737
"Yes, I did," Wukong said.

19
00:01:20.757 --> 00:01:22.758
"No, you didn't!"

20
00:01:23.178 --> 00:01:23.959
Bajie said.

21
00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:26.400
Just then his stomach growled.

22
00:01:27.041 --> 00:01:29.182
"I'll cook some food for breakfast."

23
00:01:32.396 --> 00:01:35.117
"We'll eat later, Bajie," the Tang Monk said.

24
00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:37.158
"I want to start walking."

25
00:01:39.239 --> 00:01:41.240
"Ugh," Bajie complained.

26
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.381
"All we ever do is walk!"

27
00:01:46.422 --> 00:01:48.202
They soon arrived in a mountain village.

28
00:01:54.765 --> 00:01:58.627
careful—demons could be nearby," Wukong warned the others.

29
00:01:58.647 --> 00:02:01.668
"They might want to eat the Tang Monk."

30
00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.602
As villagers smiled and waved, Wukong pulled out his iron bar.

31
00:02:08.943 --> 00:02:10.303
The Tang Monk glared at him.

32
00:02:10.323 --> 00:02:12.384
"Put that away, Wukong."

33
00:02:12.404 --> 00:02:17.066
"Master is right—this place seems safe," Sha Wujing said.

34
00:02:17.086 --> 00:02:19.807
Wukong sighed and put the bar away.

35
00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.249
travelers," a villager said.

36
00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:28.371
"Please come inside and have some breakfast."

37
00:02:30.251 --> 00:02:31.612
"That sounds wonderful!"

38
00:02:31.988 --> 00:02:33.169
Bajie said with a grin.

39
00:02:34.369 --> 00:02:35.570
The Tang Monk bowed.

40
00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.471
"Thank you very much, but we're in a hurry."

41
00:02:39.671 --> 00:02:42.192
Bajie frowned, but Wukong felt relieved.

42
00:02:42.212 --> 00:02:45.354
"I'm glad Master wants to keep walking," he thought.

43
00:02:45.374 --> 00:02:47.535
"This place seems dangerous."

44
00:02:51.336 --> 00:02:53.177
A dark cloud formed in the sky.

45
00:02:53.197 --> 00:02:57.959
"It looks like it will rain," the Tang Monk said, looking up.

46
00:02:57.979 --> 00:03:00.480
"Maybe we should stop here for breakfast."

47
00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:06.041
"That might be a demon," Wukong thought, gazing at the ominous cloud.

48
00:03:07.022 --> 00:03:08.322
He turned to his companions.

49
00:03:09.362 --> 00:03:11.223
"You wait here while I get a look at that cloud.

50
00:03:12.663 --> 00:03:15.344
Don't enter any of these houses until I return."

51
00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:24.447
is too careful sometimes," Bajie said with a snort as Wukong flew off.

52
00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:28.788
Just then the Tang Monk felt a raindrop on top of his head.

53
00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:34.852
More drops fell, and suddenly rain poured down, soaking the Tang Monk, Bajie, and Wujing.

54
00:03:35.732 --> 00:03:36.953
A villager opened his door.

55
00:03:36.973 --> 00:03:40.575
"Please come inside where it's warm and dry."

56
00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.220
let's get out of this rain," the Tang Monk said.

57
00:03:48.441 --> 00:03:50.822
He and his companions hurried into the villager's house.

58
00:03:54.064 --> 00:03:56.466
Up in the sky, Wukong approached the dark cloud.

59
00:03:57.747 --> 00:04:00.809
Hiding behind a smaller cloud, he peeked out at the dark one.

60
00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.292
A huge demon sat on it as several small demons bowed to him.

61
00:04:05.312 --> 00:04:07.953
"I knew there was a demon!"

62
00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:09.154
Wukong thought.

63
00:04:09.174 --> 00:04:16.519
"Our master, the Demon of Black Rain, is amazing," one small demon said.

64
00:04:16.539 --> 00:04:18.920
"He can make rain!"

65
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.201
another one said.

66
00:04:20.221 --> 00:04:24.844
"Yes, I can," the huge demon said with a laugh.

67
00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:29.542
"Soon we'll eat the Tang Monk and live forever!"

68
00:04:31.182 --> 00:04:33.383
The demons laughed and cheered.

69
00:04:37.525 --> 00:04:43.027
demons are dumb—rain won't hurt Master," Wukong murmured, shaking his head.

70
00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.189
He went back down to the ground.

71
00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.951
When he got there, he gasped in alarm.

72
00:04:50.971 --> 00:04:53.372
"The village is gone!"
